# Actual built-in imagegen prompt

Goal candidate: 6fa55d29-9d79-5b80-92f2-01f9bb64ef35

Use case: scientific-educational. Create a friendly abstract comic-style German chemistry learning illustration, wide landscape approximately 1600 x 900, opaque background, clear dark navy outlines, warm light classroom palette with pastel blue, green and orange. Subject: controlled physical property investigation of identified PLA plastic samples. A simple attractive laboratory bench close-up, NO people, NO hands, NO biological waste/degradation scene. Main large central apparatus: a narrow rectangular PLA test strip rests horizontally across two equally high support blocks; a small standard weight at the middle produces a modest elastic downward bend, clearly still supported at both ends. A vertical measuring scale beside the midpoint shows how the deflection is measured, without tiny numerals. In the foreground two matching-size sample strips lie side by side, plainly labelled "PLA A" and "PLA B", one pale blue and one pale green. A caliper next to them suggests matching sample thickness and geometry; no detailed caliper digits. On the right a large simple clipboard with an EMPTY raw-data table and a pencil, header "Rohdaten", only two short row labels A and B, no invented measurements, no success ticks or grades. Three sparse large words integrated tastefully as captions: "Vergleichen", "Messen", "Dokumentieren". Convey same geometry and controlled conditions, not a claim that biobased means biodegradable. Keep apparatus, sample identity and recording clear at 360-pixel total image width. No heat, flames, molten polymer, synthesis apparatus, chemical formulas, safety warning blocks, photorealism or dense text. Friendly hand-drawn didactic landscape illustration matching a modern school learning platform.
